    "field": "Global carbon cycle",
    "problem": "The mechanisms responsible for the enhancement of the terrestrial carbon sink and the resulting implications for the growth rate of atmospheric CO\u2082, a key factor in the global carbon cycle, remain unclear.",
    "method": "This study uses global carbon budget estimates, ground, atmospheric and satellite observations, and multiple global vegetation and diagnostic models to attribute a recent pause in the atmospheric CO2 growth rate to an enhanced terrestrial carbon sink driven by CO2 fertilization and a slowdown in warming-induced respiration.",
    "task": "The task is to examine the mechanisms responsible for the recent pause in the growth rate of atmospheric CO2, using multiple data sources and models to attribute it to an enhanced terrestrial carbon sink driven by CO2 fertilization and a slowdown in warming.",
